{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "File created successfully at: /sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r2-holdout/home/.claude/projects/-sandbox-runs-eval-INC-94-r2-holdout-harbor-dispatch/memory/MEMORY.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01UYRDaU3mBiacu6rewfRABq", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "sessionId": "77470992-97c2-4168-a540-884d515a2eea", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:46:41.263Z", "toolUseResult": {"content": "- [INC-94 Berth Booking Fix](inc-94-berth-booking.md) — Fixed back-to-back bookings being incorrectly rejected\n"}, "type": "user"}
{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"id": "toolu_01WpXLA3KdmRUqd5YAc1sup1", "input": {"content": "---\nname: inc-94-berth-booking\ndescription: Fixed overlap detection in BerthSchedule to allow back-to-back bookings\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n## INC-94: Back-to-back berth bookings rejected\n\nFixed in commit 19a3036 on 2026-09-28.\n\n**Problem:** The `overlaps()` function in `src/berths/schedule.ts` used `<=` comparisons, which incorrectly treated adjacent bookings (where one ends exactly when another starts) as overlapping. This prevented planners from booking consecutive vessels on the same berth.\n\n**Solution:** Changed the overlap detection from:\n```javascript\nreturn a.start.getTime() <= b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() <= a.end.getTime();\n```\n\nTo:\n```javascript\nreturn a.start.getTime() < b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() < a.end.getTime();\n```\n\nThis allows touching boundaries (where one booking ends when another starts) while still preventing true overlaps.\n\n**Testing:** Added test case \"back-to-back bookings on the same berth are accepted\" to verify the fix works correctly. All 27 tests pass.\n", "file_path": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r2-holdout/home/.claude/projects/-sandbox-runs-eval-INC-94-r2-holdout-harbor-dispatch/memory/inc-94-berth-booking.md"}, "name": "Write", "type": "tool_use"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9jkh8oyATi6dVTb4UM", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "77470992-97c2-4168-a540-884d515a2eea", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:46:45.409Z", "type": "assistant"}
{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "File created successfully at: /sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r2-holdout/home/.claude/projects/-sandbox-runs-eval-INC-94-r2-holdout-harbor-dispatch/memory/inc-94-berth-booking.md", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01WpXLA3KdmRUqd5YAc1sup1", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "sessionId": "77470992-97c2-4168-a540-884d515a2eea", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:46:45.475Z", "toolUseResult": {"content": "---\nname: inc-94-berth-booking\ndescription: Fixed overlap detection in BerthSchedule to allow back-to-back bookings\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 77470992-97c2-4168-a540-884d515a2eea\n  modified: 2026-09-28T03:46:45.467Z\n---\n\n## INC-94: Back-to-back berth bookings rejected\n\nFixed in commit 19a3036 on 2026-09-28.\n\n**Problem:** The `overlaps()` function in `src/berths/schedule.ts` used `<=` comparisons, which incorrectly treated adjacent bookings (where one ends exactly when another starts) as overlapping. This prevented planners from booking consecutive vessels on the same berth.\n\n**Solution:** Changed the overlap detection from:\n```javascript\nreturn a.start.getTime() <= b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() <= a.end.getTime();\n```\n\nTo:\n```javascript\nreturn a.start.getTime() < b.end.getTime() && b.start.getTime() < a.end.getTime();\n```\n\nThis allows touching boundaries (where one booking ends when another starts) while still preventing true overlaps.\n\n**Testing:** Added test case \"back-to-back bookings on the same berth are accepted\" to verify the fix works correctly. All 27 tests pass.\n"}, "type": "user"}
{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-94-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "Perfect! INC-94 is now complete. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Issue:** Planners couldn't book vessels onto a berth when another vessel left at that exact time. Back-to-back bookings (one ending at noon, next starting at noon) were incorrectly rejected as overlaps.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `overlaps()` function in `src/berths/schedule.ts` used `<=` comparisons, treating touching boundaries as overlaps.\n\n**Fix:** Changed the overlap detection to use `<` instead of `<=`, allowing bookings to start exactly when another ends.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Modified `src/berths/schedule.ts`: Updated overlap logic from `<=` to `<`\n- Modified `test/berths.test.ts`: Added test case for back-to-back bookings\n\n**Verification:** All 27 tests pass, including the new test confirming back-to-back bookings are accepted.\n\nCommit: `19a3036` - \"Fix back-to-back berth booking rejection (INC-94)\"", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9kK445tc1ZcSbCtjZ5", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "77470992-97c2-4168-a540-884d515a2eea", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:46:50.397Z", "type": "assistant"}
